       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p><span class=\"error\">&#91;Followup from Sourceforge Tracker&#93;</span><br/>\nFollowup Submitter: sjw46<br/>\nLogged In: YES <br/>\nuser_id=1709161<br/>\nOriginator: YES</p>\n\n<p>This problem manifests itself when policy enforcement is active and you ingest <br/>\nan object that contains a malformed/invalid policy in the object's POLICY <br/>\ndatastream. The object will ingest without any errors, but once ingested you <br/>\nare unable to access the object by either API-A or API-M because of an <br/>\nauthZException.</p>\n\n<p>The authZException is actually masking the underlying cause of the exception <br/>\nwhich is a ValidationException thrown by the parser when unable to <br/>\nsuccessfully parse the malformed policy. Repository wide policies are <br/>\nvalidated at server startup, but policies embedded in an object's POLICY <br/>\ndatastream are not parsed until an attempt is made to access the object.</p>\n\n<p>A temporary workaround should this occur is:</p>\n\n<p>1) shutdown the Fedora server<br/>\n2) edit fedora.fcfg and set the \"ENFORCE-MODE\" parameter to \"permit-all-<br/>\nrequests\"<br/>\n3) restart the server<br/>\n4) edit/remove the object with the malformed policy<br/>\n5) shutdown the server<br/>\n6) edit fedora.fcfg and set \"ENFORCE-MODE\" parameter back to \"enforce-policies\"<br/>\n7) restart the server</p>\n\n<p>------- Additional Comment #1 From Ross Wayland 2006-04-21 17:18 <span class=\"error\">&#91;reply&#93;</span> ------- <br/>\nThe proper fix for this problem is probably to just parse POLICY datastream <br/>\npolicies at the time of ingest and throw an exception if the policy is <br/>\ninvalid. Catching the problem at ingest time would prevent the object from <br/>\nbeing added to the repository.</p>\n\n<p>This will have some impact on ingest performance, so needs to be evaluated <br/>\nbefore implementing a permanent fix.</p>",
     "created": "12/Mar/07 5:24 PM",
